<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint Petersburg</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as St. Petersburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint Petersburg is a city in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neva-river">Neva River</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a> in 1703 on territory conquered from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. It was built as a purpose-built European capital and served as the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> for most of its history. Accounts of the Russian Empire treat its foundation as a symbol of Peter's westernising reforms and Russia's turn towards the Baltic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saint-petersburg.jpg" alt="Saint Petersburg" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Florstein (Telegram:WikiPhoto.Space) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_%26_Paul_fortress_in_SPB_03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
